window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-deedf2cfa71ae260"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"review-forecast-risk\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">复核销售预测风险</h1> <p>判断哪些交易应保留在承诺预测、列为上行机会，或从预测中撤下。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供预测快照、商机记录、通话笔记、交易讨论串、邮件背景、支持或法务状态、使用情况信号和负责人笔记，让它逐笔说明理由，生成有来源依据的预测风险复核。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要准备每周或每月销售预测会议的销售负责人。</li> <li>需要结合客户紧迫程度、阻碍和成交路径判断预测位置的交易复核。</li> <li>需要把有来源依据的事实与推断出的风险分开，并列出负责人后续事项的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>比较预测快照、商机数据、活动记录和交易层面的指标。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读预测文件、客户账户计划和获准使用的交易背景资料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看交易讨论串、支持情况和当前阻碍。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail（需联网）</a></td> <td>检查可能影响预测位置的客户邮件或内部邮件背景。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>复核销售预测</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请复核 [accounts or deals]，用于 [forecast period] 的预测会议。\n\n使用我提供的 CRM 商机导出文件、预测快照、通话笔记、邮件会话、Slack 交易背景、支持升级事项、法务或采购状态、使用情况信号和负责人笔记。\n\n建议哪些交易应保留在承诺预测（commit）、列为上行机会（upside），或从预测中撤下（pull）。将有来源依据的事实与推断出的风险分开，逐笔说明理由，列出阻碍和缺失背景，最后列出负责人的后续行动。不要更新 CRM 记录或更改预测。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-sales-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：销售团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/prioritize-accounts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">对客户账户排序（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"review-the-forecast-from-the-deal-record-outward\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">从交易记录出发复核预测风险</h2> <p>要评估预测风险，应将预测位置与商机详情、近期客户活动、阻碍和成交路径进行核对。提供完整复核记录，并要求 ChatGPT 为每条建议给出理由。</p> <ol> <li>明确预测周期、涉及的团队或交易，以及 commit 等预测分类的含义。</li> <li>附上 CRM 导出文件、预测快照、通话、邮件、交易讨论串、支持情况、法务、采购、使用情况和负责人笔记。</li> <li>要求 ChatGPT 区分有来源依据的事实与推断出的风险。</li> <li>使用起始提示词，检查每笔交易的理由、阻碍和下一步负责人行动。</li> <li>修改预测系统之前，先与销售负责人确认建议。</li> </ol> <p>不要只根据销售阶段推断成交把握度。可靠的复核应展示每项 commit、upside 或 pull 建议背后的证据、缺失背景、客户紧迫程度和成交路径风险。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-for-the-forecast-call\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">为预测会议做准备</h2> <p>后续可以将复核内容整理成简短的会议议程，只保留解决不确定性所需的关键问题。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this forecast review into a call agenda.\n\nGroup deals by:\n\n- commit risk\n- missing evidence\n- customer or legal blocker\n- decision needed from leadership\n- owner follow-up\n\nFor each deal, write the one question that would most reduce uncertainty. Do not change the forecast or send the agenda.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">将这份预测审阅材料整理成一份通话议程。\n\n按以下类别对交易分组：\n\n- 承诺成交风险\n- 缺失的证据\n- 客户或法律方面的阻碍\n- 需要管理层作出的决定\n- 负责人后续跟进\n\n为每笔交易写出一个最能降低不确定性的问题。不要更改预测，也不要发送议程。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"review-forecast-risk\">Review forecast risk</h1> <p>Decide which deals belong in commit, upside, or pull.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT forecast snapshots, opportunity records, call notes, deal threads, email context, support or legal status, usage signals, and owner notes, then ask it to produce a sourced forecast risk review with deal-by-deal rationale.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Sales leaders preparing a weekly or monthly forecast call.</li> <li>Deal reviews where commit position depends on customer urgency, blockers, and close path.</li> <li>Teams that need sourced facts separated from inferred risk and owner follow-ups.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Compare forecast snapshots, opportunity data, activity, and deal-level metrics.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read forecast files, account plans, and approved deal context.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Review deal threads, support context, and current blockers.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail (online)</a></td> <td>Check customer or internal email context that affects forecast position.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Review the forecast</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review [accounts or deals] for the [forecast period] forecast call.\n\nUse the CRM opportunity export, forecast snapshots, call notes, email threads, Slack deal context, support escalations, legal or procurement status, usage signals, and owner notes I provide.\n\nRecommend what should stay in commit, move to upside, or get pulled. Separate sourced facts from inferred risk, explain the rationale by deal, list blockers and missing context, and end with owner follow-ups. Do not update CRM records or change the forecast.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-sales-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Sales teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/prioritize-accounts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Prioritize accounts (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"review-the-forecast-from-the-deal-record-outward\">Review the forecast from the deal record outward</h2> <p>Forecast risk is easier to assess when the forecast position is checked against opportunity details, recent customer activity, blockers, and the close path. Give ChatGPT the full review record and require a rationale for every recommendation.</p> <ol> <li>Define the forecast period, teams or deals in scope, and commit vocabulary.</li> <li>Attach the CRM export, forecast snapshots, calls, emails, deal threads, support, legal, procurement, usage, and owner notes.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to separate sourced facts from inferred risk.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and inspect each deal's rationale, blocker, and next owner action.</li> <li>Confirm recommendations with the sales owner before changing the forecast system.</li> </ol> <p>Do not infer confidence from stage alone. A useful review shows the evidence, missing context, customer urgency, and close-path risk behind each commit, upside, or pull recommendation.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-for-the-forecast-call\">Prepare for the forecast call</h2> <p>Use a follow-up pass to turn the review into a short call agenda with the fewest questions needed to resolve uncertainty.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this forecast review into a call agenda.\n\nGroup deals by:\n\n- commit risk\n- missing evidence\n- customer or legal blocker\n- decision needed from leadership\n- owner follow-up\n\nFor each deal, write the one question that would most reduce uncertainty. Do not change the forecast or send the agenda.\n</code></pre>"};
